# {{$pkg}}

The TypeScript client of the {{.App.Label}} API, generated by esquadro from
its model: do not edit it, change the model. It needs nothing but `fetch`:
browsers, Node, Bun and edge runtimes.

## Install
{{if eq .Options.registry "github"}}
It is published to GitHub Packages with each tag `v*` of the API. In the
project that uses it, an `.npmrc` tells npm where `{{$scope}}` packages are,
with a token that may read them (`read:packages`):

```
{{$scope}}:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
```
{{else}}
It is published to npmjs with each tag `v*` of the API.
{{end}}
```sh
npm install {{$pkg}}
```

The client's version is the API's: `{{$pkg}}@1.4.0` is the client of `v1.4.0`.

## Create a client

```ts
import { createClient } from "{{$pkg}}"
{{if $realms}}
// In a browser, signed in with the {{(index $realms 0).Name}}'s session cookie (the page and
// the API on one site, e.g. app.example.com and api.example.com):
const api = createClient({ baseUrl: "https://api.example.com", auth: { cookie: "{{(index $realms 0).Name}}" } })
await api.identity.{{(index $realms 0).Entity.Camel}}.signIn({ email, password })

// On a server (Next, Astro), a client per request, with the token of
// whoever made it, never one for everyone:
const api = createClient({ baseUrl: process.env.API_URL!, token })
{{else}}
const api = createClient({ baseUrl: "https://api.example.com" })
{{end -}}
```

## Records

```ts
const page = await api.{{$e.Plural.Camel}}.list({ sort: "-created_at" })
for await (const x of api.{{$e.Plural.Camel}}.all()) { /* every one, a page at a time */ }

// Only the fields a screen shows: the type has only those.
const x = await api.{{$e.Plural.Camel}}.get(id, { fields: ["created_at"] })

// Change only what changed, on the version read: precondition_failed if
// someone changed it since.
await api.{{$e.Plural.Camel}}.patch(x.id, { /* ... */ }, { ifMatch: x })
```

`create` sends an `Idempotency-Key`: pass the same `idempotencyKey` when
retrying an operation, and it creates once. Each record says what the person
may do with it (`can`), and each list whether they may create.

## Errors and forms

```ts
import { isApiError, validate } from "{{$pkg}}"

const problems = validate.new{{$e.Pascal}}(form) // the model's rules, with the API's codes
try {
  await api.{{$e.Plural.Camel}}.create(form)
} catch (e) {
  if (isApiError(e, "invalid_fields")) showErrors(e.fields)
}
```
{{end -}}
